{
 "id": "y6-3-1-iconnect",
 "label": "6.3.1: What Is a Network?",
 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "do-now",
   "label": "Do Now: Fix the Score (1 of 2)",
   "type": "multiple-choice",
   "containerId": "y6-31-do-now",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Fix the Score (1 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does set [score] to (1) never get past 1, however many fruit you catch?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>set always puts the score to the same number. It does not add to what was there before.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Recap of 6.2.3 and 6.2.6. This is the Fruit script in a Fruit Catcher game.</p><div class=\"igame-two-col\"><div class=\"scratchblocks-card\"><pre class=\"blocks\">when flag clicked\nset [score v] to (0)\nforever\nif &lt;touching [Basket v] ?&gt; then\nset [score v] to (1)\ngo to x: (0) y: (180)\nend\nend</pre></div><div id=\"y6-31-do-now\"></div></div>",
   "items": [
    {
     "prompt": "Every catch should add 1 to the score. After three catches the score is still 1. Which block should replace set [score] to (1)?",
     "options": [
      "change [score] by (1)",
      "set [score] to (0)",
      "go to x: (0) y: (0)"
     ],
     "correct": 0,
     "explain": "set [score] to (1) puts the score back to 1 on every catch. change [score] by (1) adds 1 each time: 1, 2, 3."
    },
    {
     "prompt": "Which block sends the fruit back to the top after a catch?",
     "options": [
      "go to x: (0) y: (180)",
      "set [score] to (1)",
      "forever"
     ],
     "correct": 0,
     "explain": "go to x: (0) y: (180) moves the fruit to the middle of the top of the stage, so it can fall again."
    }
   ],
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: a variable that will not change",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "<strong>A similar script.</strong> In a Bat game, the player loses a life each time the Bat touches the Cat. The game starts with 3 lives, but lives stays at 2.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-note\">set [lives] to (3) at the flag, then set [lives] to (2) when touching Bat</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Play it in your head. Touch the Bat once: lives is set to 2.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\">lives: 3 &rarr; <span class=\"wt-hl\">2</span></p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Touch the Bat again. The same block runs: lives is set to 2 again. It never goes lower.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\">lives: 2 &rarr; <span class=\"wt-hl\">2</span></p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "A <b>set</b> block always gives the same number. To go down by one each time, the game needs a block that takes 1 away from what is already there.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\"><span class=\"wt-hl\">change [lives] by (-1)</span>: 3, 2, 1, 0</p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Now look at the Fruit Catcher script. Which block keeps putting the score to the same number, and which block would add 1 each time?",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-note\">set gives the same number; change adds to it</div>"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "do-now-2",
   "label": "Do Now: Where Does It End? (2 of 2)",
   "type": "short-answer-validation",
   "validatorId": "y6-31-do-now-2",
   "validatorKey": "y6_31_do_now_2",
   "content": "<h2 class=\"lesson-h2\">Do Now: Where Does It End? (2 of 2)</h2><details class=\"lesson-tps\"><summary><span class=\"lesson-tps-steps\">Think <b>&rarr;</b> Pair <b>&rarr;</b> Share</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-q\">Why does the block after the loop run only once, but the block inside runs many times?</span><span class=\"lesson-tps-reveal\">Show the answer</span></summary><div class=\"lesson-tps-a\"><p>Only the blocks inside the repeat are repeated. The block after it runs once, when the loop has finished.</p></div></details><p class=\"lesson-lead\">Recap of 6.2.1 and 6.2.2. Run the script in your head.</p><div class=\"lesson-do-now-columns\"><div><div class=\"scratchblocks-card\"><pre class=\"blocks\">when flag clicked\ngo to x: (0) y: (0)\nrepeat (3)\nchange x by (20)\nend\nchange y by (-30)</pre></div></div><div><div class=\"lesson-exam-card\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-responses\"><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y6-31-do-now-2-a\">What is x at the end?</label><input id=\"y6-31-do-now-2-a\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-a\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Where Does It End? (2 of 2) part a\" autocomplete=\"off\" inputmode=\"numeric\"></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-response\"><label for=\"y6-31-do-now-2-b\">What is y at the end?</label><input id=\"y6-31-do-now-2-b\" class=\"pseudocode-output-input lesson-exam-answer\" data-answer-kind=\"short\" data-answer-id=\"do-now-2-b\" aria-label=\"Do Now: Where Does It End? (2 of 2) part b\" autocomplete=\"off\" inputmode=\"numeric\"></div></div><div class=\"lesson-do-now-actions\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"donow-btn\" id=\"y6-31-do-now-2-check\">Check answers</button><strong>Total: 2 marks</strong></div><div id=\"y6-31-do-now-2-feedback\" class=\"pseudocode-feedback\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div></div></div></div>",
   "walkthrough": {
    "title": "Walk me through it: tracing a loop",
    "steps": [
     {
      "text": "<strong>A similar script.</strong> go to x: (0) y: (0), then repeat (4) with change x by (10) inside, then change y by (50) after the loop.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-note\">go to x: (0) y: (0) &middot; repeat (4) { change x by (10) } &middot; change y by (50)</div>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Start: the sprite goes to x: 0, y: 0.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\">x = 0, y = 0</p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "The loop runs 4 times. Each time, x goes up by 10: 10, 20, 30, 40.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\">x: 0 &rarr; 10 &rarr; 20 &rarr; 30 &rarr; <span class=\"wt-hl\">40</span></p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "After the loop, change y by (50) runs once: y goes from 0 to 50.",
      "visual": "<p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;text-align:center;font-size:20px;font-family:var(--font-mono, monospace)\">y: 0 &rarr; <span class=\"wt-hl\">50</span></p>"
     },
     {
      "text": "Now do the same for the Do Now script: count the loops, add up the x changes, then do the block after the loop.",
      "visual": "<div class=\"wt-note\">loop first, then the block after it</div>"
     }
    ]
   }
  },
